# Raw sequencing data — 9.8 GB, 8,840 FASTQ files. Never commit.
WBM*/
*.fq.gz
*.fastq.gz

# PFI single-page reports (~7 MB each) and the classifier taxonomy.
WBM*_en.html
Zymo/
stool_sms/
sampleInfo.xlsx

# Classifier reference lists — PFIDB_v5_0.xlsx plus the kingdom-split taxid lists.
# Vendor data, 2.3 MB, not ours to redistribute. analysis/resolve_taxids.py and
# analysis/export_rules.py read them when present and degrade gracefully when absent.
PFI_DB/

# Headless-Chrome and npx scratch from docs/img/render.sh.
Crashpad/
.com.google.Chrome.*
node-compile-cache/

# Assembly output — 71 MB, includes a 55 MB contigs FASTA and bwa-mem2 indexes.
assembly/

# Derived tables regenerated by analysis/*.py from the reports above.
analysis/*.tsv
analysis/*.json
!analysis/triage_rules.json
analysis/WBM*.json

# Generated evidence reports and exports — rebuild with `triage.py --html` and
# `export_rules.py`. The stool report additionally carries donor sample identifiers.
# docs/reference_rules.md is the diffable equivalent of the workbook and IS tracked.
analysis/triage_report*.html
analysis/triage_rules.xlsx

# Briefing decks and templates.
*.pptx
~$*

# Knowledge graph built by the graphify skill - 1.6 MB of regenerable output, and the cache
# stores absolute paths from this machine. Rebuild with `/graphify`.
graphify-out/

# Local tooling state.
.omc/
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
